      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Optional (Code Simplicity)**: Both the `CONFIG_FINGERPRINT_MCU` and non-`CONFIG_FINGERPRINT_MCU` branches duplicate the `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SPI)` check and `spi_get_protocol_info(args)` call, and accumulate the result in a mutable `ret_status` variable.\n\nUsing early returns inside the `CONFIG_FINGERPRINT_MCU` block allows both paths to share a single `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SPI)` check and eliminates the `ret_status` local variable (since this is a cherry-pick to a release branch, feel free to keep the cherry-pick identical to the upstream commit and consider this on `main`):\n\n```c\nstatic enum ec_status\nhost_command_protocol_info(struct host_cmd_handler_args *args)\n{\n\tif (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_FINGERPRINT_MCU)) {\n\t\t/*\n\t\t * Read transport type from TRANSPORT_SEL bootstrap pin the\n\t\t * first time this function is called.\n\t\t */\n\t\tif (curr_transport_type \u003d\u003d FP_TRANSPORT_TYPE_UNKNOWN)\n\t\t\tcurr_transport_type \u003d get_fp_transport_type();\n\n\t\tif (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USART_HOST_COMMAND) \u0026\u0026\n\t\t    curr_transport_type \u003d\u003d FP_TRANSPORT_TYPE_UART)\n\t\t\treturn usart_get_protocol_info(args);\n\n\t\tif (curr_transport_type !\u003d FP_TRANSPORT_TYPE_SPI)\n\t\t\treturn EC_RES_INVALID_COMMAND;\n\t}\n\n\tif (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SPI))\n\t\treturn spi_get_protocol_info(args);\n\n\treturn EC_RES_INVALID_COMMAND;\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/79b97f82-80df-4199-9b51-c2b7b91d1261)",
